        <!-- Static sections -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_ARCADIA_GATE"><Text>Awakens once you have discovered 30% of the map's Natural Wonders — then, while tall:</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_ARCADIA_AWAKENED"><Text>Awakened — you have discovered 30% of the map's Natural Wonders. While tall:</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_ALWAYS_ON"><Text>always on</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_ARCADIA_BODY"><Text>Breathtaking rural tiles each gain +1/+2/+3 (by Age) [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] [icon:YIELD_PRODUCTION] [icon:YIELD_HAPPINESS] [icon:YIELD_SCIENCE] [icon:YIELD_FOOD].[N]Buildings and Wonders gain +1/+2/+3 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] and [icon:YIELD_GOLD] per adjacent Mountain, and Mountains become workable.[N]Worked water tiles yield by type (rivers, Lakes, open sea, Reefs, water Natural Wonders), and Buildings near Coast or a Navigable River gain [icon:YIELD_GOLD] / [icon:YIELD_PRODUCTION].</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_FOUNDATIONS_GATE"><Text>Always on — no research needed, scales with your city.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_FOUNDATIONS_BODY"><Text>Bonus [icon:YIELD_HAPPINESS] Happiness and reduced Specialist upkeep that grow as your city grows, plus +3 [icon:YIELD_DIPLOMACY] Influence per turn toward your first city-states.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_GATE"><Text>Reach beyond your borders — resources are claimable up to 5 hexes from a Settlement.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_BODY"><Text>The [B]Surveyor[/B] claims one resource tile, bringing it and its yields into your borders, then retires. Build another to reach further.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_CLAIMED"><Text>Claimed</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_OF"><Text>of</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_TAIL"><Text>revealed resources within Surveyor reach (4–5 hexes out)</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SURV_NONE"><Text>No revealed resources within Surveyor reach (4–5 hexes out) yet — keep exploring.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_CONQUEST_GATE"><Text>Pays out on conquest; needs fewer than 3 total settlements.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_CONQUEST_ACTIVE"><Text>Active — going to war pays out this Age:</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_CONQUEST_BODY"><Text>Take the fight to rivals — while your empire stays small, capturing, pillaging, and razing enemy settlements each pay a bounty:</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PAYOUT_CAPTURE"><Text>First capture of a settlement pays</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PAYOUT_ONETIME"><Text>(one-time per settlement)</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PAYOUT_PILLAGE"><Text>Pillaging a conquered city's buildings pays an extra</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PAYOUT_PER_BUILDING"><Text>per building</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PAYOUT_RAZE"><Text>Razing is near-instant — a city you can't hold is gone in a turn or two.</Text></Row>
        <!-- City-States (suzerain) Core-tab panel [internal lane key stays 'protectorates']. The BODY numbers
             (per 4 pop, +2 Influence, +5 range) mirror the generator config ($suzPerPopDiv/$suzDiploAmt/
             $suzTradeRangeAmt in tools/gen-ascendant.ps1); retune both together. -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_LANE_PROTECTORATES"><Text>City-States</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PROTECTORATES_GATE"><Text>Win City-State Suzerainties to feed the metropolis.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PROTECTORATES_ACTIVE"><Text>Active — your Suzerainties feed the metropolis:</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PROTECTORATES_BODY"><Text>Suzerainty itself feeds the metropolis: for each City-State type you are Suzerain of, your cities earn +1 of its yield per 4 [icon:YIELD_POPULATION] Urban Population ([icon:YIELD_SCIENCE] Scientific, [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Cultural, [icon:YIELD_PRODUCTION] Militaristic, [icon:YIELD_GOLD] Economic, [icon:YIELD_FOOD] Expansionist) - whichever Suzerain bonus you pick. Diplomatic Suzerainties add +2 [icon:YIELD_DIPLOMACY] Influence per turn each. Each Suzerain grants +1 Resource capacity; Economic ones add +5 Trade Route range.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PROT_SUZ_OF"><Text>Suzerain of</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_PROT_NONE"><Text>Not Suzerain of any City-State yet — win one to start the yields.</Text></Row>
        <!-- Settlements tab: per-slot "what / how to get / have?" for the founding settlements + the two Charters. -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_TAB_SETTLE"><Text>Settlements</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_LANE_SETTLEMENTS"><Text>Settlements</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SETTLE_BASE_NAME"><Text>Founding Settlements</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SETTLE_BASE_BODY"><Text>Always yours — {1_Count} founding this Age (1 in Antiquity, 2 in Exploration &amp; Modern). Every settlement past these must be earned through a Charter.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SETTLE_CHARTER_HAVE"><Text>Earned — this Charter is granting you +1 Settlement.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SETTLE_CHARTER_LOCKED"><Text>Locked — earn your Expansion Triumph, {1_Triumph} ({2_Trigger}), and this Charter is granted immediately for +1 Settlement.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_SETTLE_TRIGGER_TBD"><Text>see the Triumphs tab</Text></Row>

        <!-- Empty / edge states -->
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_NO_MA"><Text>Metropolis Ascendant is not enabled in this game — nothing to display.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_ROUTE_DONE"><Text>Nothing left to unlock — every Metropolis Ascendant bonus this Age is yours.</Text></Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MAD_DRAFT_NOTE"><Text>Yield figures are the game's own attribution, read live. Bonuses without a per-turn yield (slots, caps, combat strength) show no figure.</Text></Row>
